// Title: Curl Download And Execute Combination
// Sigma ID: 21dd6d38-2b18-4453-9404-a0fe4a0cc288
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Sreeman, Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2020-01-13 | Modified: 2024-03-05
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1218, command-and-control, T1105
// Description: Adversaries can use curl to download payloads remotely and execute them. Curl is included by
//   default in Windows 10 build 17063 and later.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://medium.com/@reegun/curl-exe-is-the-new-rundll32-exe-lolbin-3f79c5f35983
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_cmd_curl_download_exec_combo.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains " -c " or ProcessCommandLine contains " /c " or ProcessCommandLine contains " –c " or ProcessCommandLine contains " —c " or ProcessCommandLine contains " ―c ") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "curl " and ProcessCommandLine contains "http" and ProcessCommandLine contains "-o" and ProcessCommandLine contains "&")
